sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Customer
    participant Client as Customer Channel
    participant API as Agent API
    participant Security as Authentication / Security
    participant Session as Strands File Session Manager
    participant Agent as Agent Orchestrator
    participant Banking as Banking API
    participant KB as Knowledge Base
    participant Handoff as Handoff Component

    Customer->>Client: Send message
    Client->>API: POST /api/agent/chat with message and optional session_id
    API->>Security: Authenticate request and establish trusted identity
    Security-->>API: Trusted identity context

    alt Authentication fails
        API-->>Client: 401 authentication error
        Client-->>Customer: Ask customer to authenticate
    else Authentication succeeds
        alt New conversation (session_id omitted)
            API->>Session: Create session bound to authenticated customer
            Session-->>API: New session_id
        else Existing conversation
            API->>Session: Load session and verify ownership against trusted identity
            alt Session invalid or inaccessible
                Session-->>API: Reject access
                API-->>Client: Safe session-unavailable error
                Client-->>Customer: Explain conversation is unavailable
            else Session is valid
                Session-->>API: Existing conversation state
            end
        end

        opt Session is available
            API->>Session: Append customer message and load conversation context
            Session-->>API: Conversation context
            API->>Agent: Process message with trusted identity and session context
            Agent->>Agent: Classify intent and determine required path

            alt Policy or product question
                Agent->>KB: Retrieve relevant passages
                KB-->>Agent: Passages with document and section metadata
                Agent->>Agent: Assess evidence sufficiency and consistency
                alt Evidence is sufficient
                    Agent->>Agent: Compose answer with source citations
                else Evidence is insufficient or conflicting
                    Agent->>Agent: Abstain from guessing
                    opt Handoff requested or appropriate
                        Agent->>Handoff: Submit handoff request and concise summary
                        Handoff-->>Agent: Handoff acceptance or failure
                    end
                end
            else Account-specific or banking request
                Agent->>Agent: Select approved tool and validate tool input
                Agent->>Banking: Request operation; customer identity comes from trusted context
                Banking-->>Agent: Result, denial, pending confirmation, or unresolved outcome
                Note over Agent,Banking: Backend authorization and confirmation rules are authoritative.
            else Clarification needed
                Agent->>Agent: Prepare focused clarification question
            else Human support requested or required
                Agent->>Handoff: Submit handoff request and concise summary
                Handoff-->>Agent: Handoff acceptance or failure
            end

            Agent->>Session: Persist assistant reply and updated conversation state
            Session-->>Agent: Persistence result
            Agent-->>API: Reply, status, citations if applicable, and session_id
            API-->>Client: Chat response
            Client-->>Customer: Display reply and next step
        end
    end

    Note over Security,Banking: A session_id identifies a conversation; it is not proof of identity.
    Note over Session,Banking: Conversation history is stored by the session manager; banking records and pending confirmations remain authoritative in PostgreSQL via the Banking API.
    Note over Agent: A completed conversation turn does not by itself prove that a banking operation succeeded.
